<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>France 24 - International breaking news, top stories and headlines</title><subtitle type="html">Breaking news and world news from France 24 on Business, Sports, Culture. Video news. News from the US, Europe, Asia Pacific, Africa, Middle East, America</subtitle><id>https://www.france24.com/en/rss</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/rss" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Live: Russia hits Kyiv’s Southern Bridge as Moscow continues to pound capital</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:82c65aef7f8a9e24a7fdcaef050498219c19dbf7918b7ed54c49d621c28c8b4a</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T05:30:42Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261002-live-russia-hits-kyiv-s-southern-bridge-as-moscow-continues-to-pound-capital" /><summary type="html">Russian airstrikes hit Kyiv’s Southern Bridge, the city’s mayor said on Friday. Russia also targeted a school and apartment buildings in the capital, killing at least one person. Ukraine, meanwhile, launched an overnight drone attack on the Russian city of Volgograd, targeting industrial facilities. Follow our liveblog for all the latest developments on the war in Ukraine.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Saudi-led coalition accuses Houthis of striking Medina power station</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:19afad4ce1ba20544d00ebffb8ea0d6a690e6b840edf840db231718ddd472f80</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T02:39:43Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-saudi-led-coalition-houthis-striking-medina-power-station" /><summary type="html">Yemen’s Iran-backed Houthis struck an electricity distribution station supplying the Prophet’s Mosque in Saudi Arabia’s holy city of Medina, the Saudi-led coalition said Thursday, drawing condemnation across the Muslim world. The Houthis denied involvement in the drone attack, which came as fighting intensified between government forces and rebels in Yemen.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>More than half of Europe faced intense summer heat stress, EU monitor says</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:46e3961347985907de252a17c8024bd93da2d9137fb252246f23889fd6a799b2</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T02:18:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/environment/20261002-europe-summer-heat-stress-eu-monitor" /><summary type="html">A record 52% of Europe faced intense heat stress this summer, the EU’s climate monitor said Friday, as climate change fuelled widespread heatwaves and tens of thousands of excess deaths. Europe recorded its third warmest summer, while western Europe experienced its hottest, with several countries setting national temperature records overall.</summary><category term="Environment" /></entry><entry><title>G20 trade ministers deadlocked over industrial overcapacity, says US trade chief</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ea9ace9909a9e8aeb640a7155746aff81bfd608d4658df50f37b5c03dcea5c77</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-02T01:30:05Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/economy/20261002-g20-trade-ministers-overcapacity-impasse-greer" /><summary type="html">G20 trade ministers failed to agree on tackling excess industrial capacity and eliminating forced labour from supply chains, US Trade Representative Jamieson Greer said Thursday. Speaking during talks in Milwaukee, Greer highlighted overcapacity, a criticism often directed at China, which rejects it. The United States holds this year's rotating presidency.</summary><category term="Economy" /></entry><entry><title>Netanyahu says Flydubai co-pilot was radicalised as UAE probes terror link</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f60d5a6758695602e74ecbd14a632a43f1ae5eee029377020dfd0acfe05bf110</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T23:27:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261001-netanyahu-flydubai-co-pilot-uae-terror-link" /><summary type="html">Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu said Thursday the co-pilot accused of attacking a Flydubai flight carrying mostly Israelis had undergone “Islamist radical indoctrination”, as UAE authorities investigated a possible terror link. The captain and passengers overpowered the suspect before the plane made an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia on Wednesday.</summary><category term="Middle East" /></entry><entry><title>French investigative site says antisemitic messages tied to Jordan Bardella, Le Pen's ally</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1e34fdb3c86701ccbafdd72de4a6696b27d649eb00a60c90c903cd5b00448777</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:41:38Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/france/20261001-jordan-bardella-antisemitic-messages-authenticated-french-outlet" /><summary type="html">French investigative outlet Mediapart said on Thursday it had authenticated antisemitic messages allegedly sent by far-right politician Jordan Bardella in 2013. Bardella denied writing them and said he would sue for defamation and forgery. The allegations come seven months before France’s presidential election, with Marine Le Pen leading opinion polls.</summary><category term="France" /></entry><entry><title>Migration deal: 'Really a scheme around political diplomacy between UK &amp; France in post-Brexit era'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c0dce6bff74ee805b173ad3b204389798b722b0a5cdee4fbd7161e2eed2151d</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:27:09Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-migration-deal-really-a-scheme-around-political-diplomacy-between-uk-france-in-post-brexit-era-1" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Parvati Nair, Professor of Hispanic, Cultural and Migration Studies at Queen Mary University of London. She sees the UK-France migration agreement as a small but revealing element of a much wider post-Brexit relationship, in which questions of migration are intertwined with diplomacy, security, intelligence and surveillance. She warns that the scheme risks trivialising a complex human plight it into deterrence and a numbers game. She argues humans have always moved, and migration can profoundly enrich societies. The challenge is to build systems that recognise both national sovereignty and human dignity.</summary></entry><entry><title>US presses Europe to release diesel reserves 'immediately' as Trump threatens export ban</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:77e81b8f326551b5847b6d38cf32a820219103c97d5292cbcecba6f36aad05ee</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T22:08:51Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-us-europe-diesel-reserves-fuel-prices" /><summary type="html">The United States on Thursday urged European allies to release strategic diesel reserves immediately to curb prices driven higher by the US war on Iran. EU states will discuss a coordinated response on Friday, as Washington increases pressure following US President Donald Trump's suggestion that he could ban US diesel exports.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>Fake BBC report falsely implicates Indian passenger and pilot in Flydubai hijacking attempt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:abeac53f0f9a24a396a11ab5f165a57078529c093f213361c6917c2226b5019e</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T21:11:44Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fake-bbc-report-falsely-implicates-indian-passenger-and-pilot-in-flydubai-hijacking-attempt" /><summary type="html">False videos are circulating after the attempted hijacking of a Flydubai flight between Dubai and Tel Aviv. One fake “BBC” report falsely claims an Indian passenger was behind the incident and links him to the stabbed pilot, Smit Machchhar. The video though, is an AI-generated deepfake: the BBC never broadcast it, and its footage and audio were doctored. A second clip was also misrepresented and filmed in Dubai, not over where the incident occurred. Vedika Bahl fact-checks in Truth or Fake.</summary><category term="Truth or Fake" /></entry><entry><title>'Fundamental demand': Saint-Denis students seek same opportunity as those in 'more privileged areas'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3dabe61ac5ffbfe4f10cfb3c551f4631e674b79076b0e7e002015fb9de900474</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T21:02:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.france24.com/en/fundamental-demand-saint-denis-students-seek-same-opportunity-as-those-in-more-privileged-areas" /><summary type="html">Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome a high school teacher who agreed to speak with us anonymously as protests intensify at a high school in a northern Paris suburb. The protests are shining a cruel light on major problems that have existed for years. All the while, police are cracking down on students, using teargas and strongarm tactics as students blockade entrances. For this high school teacher, the protests reflect concerns about everyday conditions in which students are expected to learn. Their demands are not abstract political claims. They are asking for an environment that allows them to learn effectively.</summary></entry><entry><title>Ethiopia and Eritrea break diplomatic ties over conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6e2c28fb9b9aa9ab3e48f651c3e0e45b00adaf6693b2a429d249f3d43f4790f1</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T20:28:30Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-and-eritrea-break-diplomatic-ties-over-conflict--12a4e73260b2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/ethiopia-and-eritrea-break-diplomatic-ties-over-conflict" /><summary type="html">In tonight's edition, Ethiopia and Eritrea break diplomatic ties, accusing each other of stoking internal conflicts. Also, Nigeria rolls out a digital postcode system for every building. And I speak to one of the co-founders of the he Rural Women’s Assembly as it is recognised for its work challenging power systems.</summary><category term="Eye on Africa" /></entry><entry><title>UK police arrest dual UK-Iranian national over Fairford air base incident</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ae51894d2d319b5d8a33e3c91b495e32bab3a5b6af8f682cbbf2aead11444fd4</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T19:40:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident--eddc8f085ba4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/europe/20261001-uk-police-arrest-dual-uk-iranian-national-over-fairford-air-base-incident" /><summary type="html">British police on Thursday arrested a British-Iranian dual national in connection with the security incident at the Fairford airbase Wednesday. Five other men initially arrested over the incidence were later released without charge on bail.</summary><category term="Europe" /></entry><entry><title>France’s purchasing power crisis: Navigating the pinch</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a2814896ca5094f4815e7c038b131cb66c1c4cbff3437b53e79a3284ab689edb</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T19:26:18Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/economy/20261001-france-s-purchasing-power-crisis-navigating-the-pinch--b9a1f8c10741.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/economy/20261001-france-s-purchasing-power-crisis-navigating-the-pinch" /><summary type="html">With looming elections and a draft budget that aims to address a €305.7bn financing requirement, French households are increasingly in the red. Will wages ever manage to outpace energy inflation?</summary><category term="Economy" /></entry><entry><title>'Guilty of all charges': Man City at centre of 'biggest scandal in football history', vows to appeal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f8f798fe0ba8ea72190c16dd57093a6b344e0c4a67ad058e5f2be5212ebe11d6</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T16:37:15Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261001-guilty-of-all-charges-man-city-at-centre-of-biggest-scandal-in-football-history-vows-to-app--8c015176048c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/spotlight/20261001-guilty-of-all-charges-man-city-at-centre-of-biggest-scandal-in-football-history-vows-to-appeal" /><summary type="html">François Picard is pleased to welcome our sports editor, James Vasina, and Andreas Evargora, sports journalist and commentator. Evargora describes the current Manchester City case as unprecedented in scale: “This is nothing of the scale that we’ve seen before.” The case brings together an explosive mix of pressures confronting modern sport like never before: the multibillion-euro business of football, the legal and regulatory mechanisms designed to govern it, and the increasingly complex relationship between sport, political power and international investment.</summary><category term="Spotlight" /></entry><entry><title>Students face riot police as protests over school conditions escalate in France</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1d3d8e63ce19584b8b9ffd8019581fb2fe4e02b71c664d5c5683e0b8a9c997cc</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T15:42:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/students-face-riot-police-as-protests-over-school-conditions-escalate-in-france--2f89252a49c4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/students-face-riot-police-as-protests-over-school-conditions-escalate-in-france" /><summary type="html">French teenagers on Tuesday set fire to rubbish bins and threw projectiles at police who responded with batons and tear gas, as pupils kept up blockades and protests at hundreds of high schools, demanding better conditions. The movement in the lycees, attended by students aged 15 to 18 for their final three years of secondary education in France, has angered the government.</summary></entry><entry><title>Teens block high schools across France, demand better conditions</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a0e597e1bbd6514b06ac3ba69768d36ea36e9b7cd47f5ec35ca4c045f8eee4ed</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T15:25:57Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-teens-block-high-schools-across-france-demand-better-conditions--656527cb1b55.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-teens-block-high-schools-across-france-demand-better-conditions" /><summary type="html">France's prime minister convened a crisis meeting on Thursday and canceled ministers' trips to focus on the nationwide spread of protests, some violent, by high school students venting against under-resourced schools, long hours and other complaints. The demonstrations erupted in Paris-region schools last week and have snowballed, with police making hundreds of arrests in clashes with the young protesters. FRANCE 24's International Affairs Editor Angela Diffley tells us more.</summary></entry><entry><title>Rethinking traditional designs: A French twist on the kimono</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:50865bac2438ee4890da9d7abae191fb18f021772d2b6c942cf43eb2551a7505</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T15:16:45Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261001-rethinking-traditional-designs-a-french-twist-on-the-kimono--bf613d3951e7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/entre-nous/20261001-rethinking-traditional-designs-a-french-twist-on-the-kimono" /><summary type="html">In this episode of Entre Nous, Delano D'Souza welcomes Alice Kith, a Paris-based designer reimagining the traditional kimono through a contemporary French lens. Her brand A-Kith brings together heritage, craftsmanship and modern Parisian style. From Poiret to Kenzo, we explore influences and how the kimono is woven into the history of Parisian fashion.</summary><category term="Entre Nous" /></entry><entry><title>Cameroon govt announces payments as teachers strike continues</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fa795b72ae90f9a0b41bbb246d235c3b5415fc31eff35f901a7239296485b683</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:56:25Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-cameroon-govt-announces-payments-as-teachers-strike-continues--2797b31873b4.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-cameroon-govt-announces-payments-as-teachers-strike-continues" /><summary type="html">In Cameroon, the start of the academic year for Universities, scheduled for October 5, may not take place. This is as a result of an indefinite strike launched by SYNES, the National Union of Higher Education Teachers. Teachers are demanding the payment of 16 billion CFA francs in academic bonuses, equivalent to nearly 24 million euros.</summary></entry><entry><title>A blessing or a curse? New Caledonia's dwindling nickel industry</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a8d55006b9f19f21e93da4456adc9ba856b2a81f6404b86a9ae185e280e9a8dc</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:39:34Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry--cc6e1bce2bc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261001-a-blessing-or-a-curse-new-caledonia-s-dwindling-nickel-industry" /><summary type="html">This Thursday October 1, the French government is holding a summit aimed at attracting investors and revitalising wealth creation in France's overseas territories. Among the assets Paris wants to highlight is New Caledonian nickel. But the industry has been severely weakened by the political deadlock and tensions that have rocked the archipelago in recent years.</summary><category term="Focus" /></entry><entry><title>Sheer devastation: '80 percent of Gazan infrastructure has been destroyed'</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:01981196183fafb08cf61fdfeb6ffa1783b56a1e8a626c15149759748010ad0d</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:16:41Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed--aa956df4e191.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/sheer-devastation-80-percent-of-gazan-infrastructure-has-been-destroyed" /><summary type="html">New images posted this week by Google Maps show the utter destruction in Gaza. It's been estimated that 61 tonnes of rubble need to be cleared – that's 20 times the amount of rubble generated in all wars across the world over the last 18 years.</summary><category term="Perspective" /></entry><entry><title>From Billie Eilish to Cardi B: Hassan Hajjaj on the stars who stepped into his colourful world</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e845ec3dba84abb92125bc74aea806be713ba2ac134d7a5255fc9ae86af49058</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:06:04Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261001-from-billie-eilish-to-cardi-b-hassan-hajjaj-on-the-stars-who-stepped-into-his-colourful-wor--1edbf8b97dd6.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/arts24/20261001-from-billie-eilish-to-cardi-b-hassan-hajjaj-on-the-stars-who-stepped-into-his-colourful-world" /><summary type="html">Moroccan-British artist and photographer Hassan Hajjaj has photographed some of the biggest names in music and pop culture – from Madonna, Billie Eilish and Alicia Keys to Cardi B and Lee "Scratch" Perry. Now, 40 of his vibrant "Rock Stars" are on show at Paris's Philharmonie. Hajjaj tells us how he creates his instantly recognisable portraits, blends Moroccan heritage with London street culture – and what happens when a global superstar steps in front of his camera.</summary><category term="arts24" /></entry><entry><title>Behind the scenes of Céline Dion's high-tech gig - Tech 24</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e4103c450c561fbbbed3b21d62c41ef4db5e96baf03fc089929a1dfc2543e8d2</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T14:03:33Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-behind-the-scenes-of-c_line-dion-s-high-tech-gig-tech-24--d0c3104b48fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-behind-the-scenes-of-c%C3%A9line-dion-s-high-tech-gig-tech-24" /><summary type="html">🎤 #CélineDion is making her great comeback with a 16-day residency in #France after years of illness. To keep her stage quiet and her voice crisp, her team is using both AI and high-tech sound systems.
 
#FRANCE24's Peter O'Brien went behind the scenes at the invitation of French audio company L-Acoustics ☝️</summary></entry><entry><title>UK, France end 'on in, one out' Channel migrant exchange deal</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:228fdc168cefd49d394bc3667d223882abc55c5c97a6dc9cefa6b0613edc9560</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:44:39Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-uk-france-end-on-in-one-out-channel-migrant-exchange-deal--d86e46b7757d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-uk-france-end-on-in-one-out-channel-migrant-exchange-deal" /><summary type="html">A year-old deal between France and Britain to return migrants crossing the Channel illegally on small boats has come to an end, the UK interior ministry said Wednesday. The deal was agreed under former UK prime minister Keir Starmer last year in a bid to help a post-Brexit reset by easing what had become a major source of tension between the neighbours.</summary></entry><entry><title>France demands belt-tightening in 2027 budget as investors sour on its debt</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8196ff28da9d252b7da896cdfa6e36302b9c2998ffbf711b6ff1a6eb0a01b9c3</id><updated>2026-10-02T05:53:25Z</updated><published>2026-10-01T13:42:54Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-demands-belt-tightening-in-2027-budget-as-investors-sour-on-its-debt--bf1952c0ff96.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261001-france-demands-belt-tightening-in-2027-budget-as-investors-sour-on-its-debt" /><summary type="html">France presented its ​2027 budget bill on Thursday, seeking to enact unpopular belt-tightening measures that can lower its deficit and appease increasingly twitchy bond investors ahead of next year's presidential election. The legislation faces a tough ride in a deeply divided parliament, as political clans position themselves for one of the country's most consequential elections in modern times.</summary></entry></feed>
